      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowers%2C_Delaware"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1734, John Bowers acquired the tract, and the area adopted the name Bowers Beach.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bowers_delaware"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Fourteen Foot Bank Light and Saxton United Methodist Church are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowers%2C_Delaware"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bowers Beach enjoys a humid subtropical climate, with warm summers and mild winters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://delaware.wiki/a/Bowers_Beach"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The beach itself stretches several miles along the Atlantic, drawing swimmers, sunbathers, kayakers, and paddleboarders.",
